1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,119
Host: So you left the VC world and went solo. What was the moment you decided?

2
00:00:05,519 --> 00:00:09,273
Guest: Honestly it was one board meeting. I realized nobody in that room had shipped anything in a year.

3
00:00:09,673 --> 00:00:15,928
Host: That is brutal.

4
00:00:16,328 --> 00:00:19,690
Guest: And I thought, if I am going to work this hard, I want to own the outcome.

5
00:00:20,090 --> 00:00:25,770
Host: So how did open source turn into customers?

6
00:00:26,170 --> 00:00:30,998
Guest: The plugin got stars first. Then companies asked for support. That was the whole funnel.

7
00:00:31,398 --> 00:00:34,688
Host: Wait, no ads, no outbound?

8
00:00:35,088 --> 00:00:40,625
Guest: Zero. The README was the landing page for two years.

9
00:00:41,025 --> 00:00:44,213
Host: Okay that is insane. Let's talk numbers.

10
00:00:44,613 --> 00:00:49,781
Guest: Right now it is a bit over twenty five k a month, solo, no funding.

11
00:00:50,181 --> 00:00:53,530
Host: And your biggest mistake?

12
00:00:53,930 --> 00:00:57,384
Guest: Building features nobody paid for. I had a roadmap of ghosts.

13
00:00:57,784 --> 00:01:02,906
Host: A roadmap of ghosts. I am stealing that.

14
00:01:03,306 --> 00:01:10,441
Guest: Take it. Every founder has one.

15
00:01:10,841 --> 00:01:14,460
Host: What would you tell someone who is on a VC startup right now and wants out?

16
00:01:14,860 --> 00:01:18,976
Guest: Ship one small thing that makes money before you quit. One. Then you have proof.

17
00:01:19,376 --> 00:01:25,513
Host: Proof beats permission.

18
00:01:25,913 --> 00:01:33,652
Guest: Exactly. Nobody gives you permission.

